nce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over unordered pairs of vertices, n · Σ_{i≥2} 1\/λᵢ over the Laplacian","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spectrum; nil when the graph is not connected, 0 for zero or one vertex.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"effectiveGraphResistance","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":"? ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryFloatingPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SB"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"N · tr(L_g⁻¹) − 1ᵀ L_g⁻¹ 1 with L_g the Laplacian grounded at the vertex of largest degree,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its GTH elimination (as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numberOfSpanningTrees"},{"type":"text","text":"): every term is a sum of positive ones,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the result keeps a relative accuracy of about n² · 10⁻¹⁶ under any weight spread, whe